- The integer array parameter `gas` and the integer array parameter `cost` must have the same length.
- All values in the integer array parameter `gas` and the integer array parameter `cost` are greater than or equal to 0 and are less than or equal to 10000.
- The integer result is the starting gas station's index if it is possible to travel around the circuit once in the clockwise direction.
- If it is not possible to travel around the circuit once in the clockwise direction, the integer result is -1.